The legal texts come from GhaLII, the Ghana Legal Information Institute (on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  GhaLII, https://ghalii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as GhaLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting GhaLII as the source (https://ghalii.org/terms-of-use/, s. 9: "you may freely use, re-use and redistribute works from GhaLII provided you credit GhaLII as your source and your use is not for commercial gain").
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: GhaLII, the Ghana Legal Information Institute (https://ghalii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws GhaLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither GhaLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
